mation of skewed features\n# Feature name: Log_Heavy_atom_sum\n# Feature description: Logarithm of the heavy atom sum.\n# Usefulness: Features like Heavy_atom_sum have a positive range and may exhibit skewness. Applying a logarithmic transformation can reduce skewness, making the feature distribution more Gaussian-like, which can improve model performance, especially for linear models and some tree-based models.\n\ndf['Log_Heavy_atom_sum'] = np.log1p(df['Heavy_atom_sum'])\n```end\n\n```python\n# Step 3: Group-based aggregation\n# Feature name: Mean_Psi_by_nCp\n# Feature description: Groupwise mean of Psi_i_A aggregated by nCp (number of terminal primary C(sp3)).\n# Usefulness: Averaging Psi_i_A (descriptor tied to pseudoconnectivity and intrinsic state) by the number of terminal primary carbons nCp may uncover meaningful local patterns within molecular substructures, enabling the model to leverage size-normalized intrinsic connectivity signals.\n\ndf['Mean_Psi_by_nCp'] = df.groupby('nCp')['Psi_i_A'].transform('mean')\n```end\n\n```python\n# Explanation why the column Reciprocal_LOC is dropped\n# Reciprocal_LOC contains a value range with an extremely high upper bound (e.g., 1,000,000,000), leading to potential issues with numerical stability during model training.\n# Given that this feature also appears redundant (it is likely a modification of LOC or another Laplacian eigenvalue related descriptor), we drop it.\n\ndf.drop(columns=['Reciprocal_LOC'], inplace=True)\n```end\n\n```python\n# Explanation why the column NssssC is dropped\n# The NssssC feature has a mean near zero and extremely low density of non-zero values (mean = 0.2828, median = 0.0, Q3 = 0.0).\n# Features with such sparse distributions often provide negligible variance for predictive tasks and may contribute noise.\n\ndf.drop(columns=['NssssC'], inplace=True)\n```end\n\n```python\n# Explanation why the column nArNO2 is dropped\n# The nArNO2 feature, representing the number of aromatic nitro groups, ha